<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahmad al-Mansur</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahmad al-Mansur was the Saadi sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> from 1578 to 1603, enriched by his victory over the Portuguese at Alcácer Quibir. Seeking control of West African gold and salt, he sent an army equipped with firearms across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a>, which defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songhai-empire">Songhai Empire</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tondibi">Battle of Tondibi</a> in 1591. The invasion led to the collapse of Songhai.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ahmad-al-mansur.jpg" alt="Ahmad al-Mansur" width="320" height="392" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: André Thevet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ahmad_al-Mansur_by_Andr%C3%A9_Thevet.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
